@page "/demo/text-inputs"
@using FlexCore.Showcase.Components.Shared
@using FlexCore.Showcase.Data

@* 2026-10-25: new page on FeatureDemoLayout; two examples (traveller details, notes with a limit). Facts checked against
   TextBoxControl.razor(.css), TextBoxTypingBehavior.cs, TextContextMenuModels.cs, NumericTextBoxControl.razor(.css),
   TextAreaControl.razor(.css), TextAreaScrollBars.cs, Editor/TextAreaControl.razor, PasswordControl.razor,
   Forms/FormItemControl.razor and wwwroot/textbox-control.js in FlexCore 0.2.49, plus Blazor's blazor.web.js 10.0.2 for how
   the value property is written. Both namespaces Fx.ControlKit and Fx.ControlKit.Editor are imported site-wide and each has a
   TextAreaControl, so this page writes Fx.ControlKit.TextAreaControl in full. Neither NumericTextBoxControl nor TextAreaControl
   captures unmatched attributes, so every field is labelled by a wrapping <label>. *@

<PageTitle>Blazor TextBox, Numeric TextBox and TextArea — FlexCore</PageTitle>

<FeatureDemoLayout Title="Text inputs" Category="Components" CategoryHref="components"
                   ControlName="TextBoxControl · NumericTextBoxControl · TextAreaControl"
                   Tagline="Single-line text, typed numbers and multi-line notes, each bound two ways to a string or a number."
                   SourcePath="TextBoxControl.razor; NumericTextBoxControl.razor; TextAreaControl.razor">
    <Overview>
        <p>
            <code>TextBoxControl</code> is a text box bound to a <code>string</code>, or a <code>&lt;textarea&gt;</code> with
            <code>Multiline</code>. By default it reports <code>ValueChanged</code> when the field changes (Tab out, click away, Enter);
            <code>UpdateOnInput</code> reports every keystroke instead. <code>NumericTextBoxControl&lt;TValue&gt;</code> is a number input
            for <code>int</code>, <code>decimal</code>, <code>double</code> or <code>float</code> that parses the text, clamps it to
            <code>Min</code> and <code>Max</code> and reports only when the entry is committed with Enter, Tab or a click away.
            <code>TextAreaControl</code> is the multi-line box with a character limit, spell checking, scroll-bar modes and methods that
            insert text at the caret and move focus.
        </p>
        <p>
            All three render native elements and bind with <code>@@bind-Value</code>. None draws a label; the fields here sit inside a
            <code>&lt;label&gt;</code>.
        </p>
    </Overview>

    <Examples>
        <DemoExample Id="details" Title="Traveller details" RazorCode="@Code.Details" CSharpCode="@Code.DetailsCs" CssCode="@Code.DetailsCss">
            <Description><p>Name has <code>UpdateOnInput</code>, so its count goes up with every keystroke; Email keeps the default and reports when the field changes: on Tab, a click away or Enter. Travellers clamps quietly: type 20 and it commits as 12. Budget rejects instead: below $250 a head its <code>ValueChange</code> handler sets <code>Cancel</code>, which leaves your figure in the box, marks it <code>aria-invalid</code> and puts focus back. <code>Format="C2"</code> shows 3200.00 in the box, because the control turns <code>C</code> into <code>F</code> for the number input; the summary adds the dollar sign.</p></Description>
            <Demo>
                <div class="details">
                    <label class="field">
                        <span class="field-label">Lead traveller</span>
                        <TextBoxControl @bind-Value="_name" @bind-Value:after="CountName" UpdateOnInput="true"
                                        Placeholder="Full name as on the passport" MaxLength="40" CssClass="text-field" />
                    </label>
                    <label class="field">
                        <span class="field-label">Email</span>
                        <TextBoxControl @bind-Value="_email" @bind-Value:after="CountEmail" InputType="email"
                                        Placeholder="name@example.com" MaxLength="80" CssClass="text-field" />
                    </label>
                    <label class="field">
                        <span class="field-label">Travellers (1 to 12)</span>
                        <NumericTextBoxControl TValue="int" @bind-Value="_travellers" Min="1" Max="12" Width="90px" />
                    </label>
                    <label class="field">
                        <span class="field-label">Budget in dollars, steps of 50</span>
                        <NumericTextBoxControl TValue="decimal" Value="_budget" ValueChange="CheckBudget"
                                               Format="C2" Step="50" Min="0" Width="140px" />
                    </label>
                </div>
                <p class="summary">
                    <strong>@Trip.Name</strong>, @Trip.Nights nights: @(string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_name) ? "no lead traveller yet" : _name),
                    @(string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_email) ? "no email yet" : _email), @_travellers travellers,
                    budget @_budget.ToString("$#,##0") (@((_budget / _travellers).ToString("$#,##0")) a head)
                </p>
                <p class="counts">ValueChanged so far: name @_nameUpdates, email @_emailUpdates</p>
                <p class="warn" role="status">@_budgetNote</p>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Id="notes" Title="Notes with a limit" RazorCode="@Code.Notes" CSharpCode="@Code.NotesCs">
            <Description><p>A 200-character note bound with <code>UpdateOnInput</code>, so the count follows every keystroke; the browser stops typing at <code>MaxLength</code>. The first button calls <code>InsertTextAsync</code>, which puts the phrase at the caret, or over the selection, although the click moved focus to the button; when the phrase would not fit it returns <code>false</code> and inserts nothing. <code>SpellCheck="true"</code> asks the browser to mark misspellings. The switch turns on the control's own context menu with the <code>Editing</code> items; it replaces the browser's menu, spelling suggestions included.</p></Description>
            <Demo>
                <div class="notes">
                    <label class="field">
                        <span class="field-label">Booking note for @Trip.Name</span>
                        <Fx.ControlKit.TextAreaControl @ref="_noteBox" @bind-Value="_note" UpdateOnInput="true" MaxLength="NoteLimit" Rows="5"
                                                       SpellCheck="true" Placeholder="Dietary needs, room requests, arrival times"
                                                       UseClassicContextMenu="_classicMenu" ContextMenuItems="TextContextMenuItems.Editing" />
                    </label>
                    <div class="note-bar">
                        <span class="count @(NoteLimit - NoteLength <= 20 ? "near" : null)">@NoteLength / @NoteLimit characters</span>
                        <ButtonControl OnClick="InsertTransfer">Insert "Airport transfer requested."</ButtonControl>
                        <ButtonControl OnClick="FocusNote">Focus the note</ButtonControl>
                        <SwitchControl @bind-Checked="_classicMenu" Label="Classic context menu" />
                    </div>
                    <p class="warn" role="status">@_noteStatus</p>
                </div>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>
    </Examples>

    <Vocabulary>
        <DocSections>
            <DocSection Id="doc-textboxcontrol-parameters" Title="TextBoxControl parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.TextBox.Length, "parameters")' Open="true">
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="TextBoxControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.TextBox" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-textboxcontrol-password-parameters" Title="TextBoxControl password parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Password.Length, "parameters")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="TextBoxControl password parameters" Rows="Vocab.Password" />
                <p>These apply when <code>InputType="password"</code> on a single-line box. <code>PasswordControl</code> wraps a <code>TextBoxControl</code> with the same mask and eye button for password fields.</p>
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-textboxcontrol-events" Title="TextBoxControl events" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.TextBoxEvents.Length, "events")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Events" Title="TextBoxControl events" Rows="Vocab.TextBoxEvents" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-textboxcontrol-methods" Title="TextBoxControl methods" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.TextBoxMethods.Length, "methods")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Methods" Title="TextBoxControl methods" Rows="Vocab.TextBoxMethods" />
                <p><code>CommitClientBufferedTypingAsync</code> and <code>OnPasteTruncatedAsync</code> are public only so the control's script can call them.</p>
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-numerictextboxcontrol-parameters" Title="NumericTextBoxControl parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Numeric.Length, "parameters")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="NumericTextBoxControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.Numeric" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-numerictextboxcontrol-events" Title="NumericTextBoxControl events" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.NumericEvents.Length, "events")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Events" Title="NumericTextBoxControl events" Rows="Vocab.NumericEvents" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-numericchangeeventargs" Title="NumericChangeEventArgs" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.NumericArgs.Length, "properties")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Properties" Title="NumericChangeEventArgs" Rows="Vocab.NumericArgs" />
                <p>The class is nested inside the control, so a handler names it in full: <code>NumericTextBoxControl&lt;decimal&gt;.NumericChangeEventArgs&lt;decimal&gt;</code>, as the budget example does.</p>
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-textareacontrol-parameters" Title="TextAreaControl parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.TextArea.Length, "parameters")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="TextAreaControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.TextArea" />
                <p>A second, simpler <code>TextAreaControl</code> lives in <code>Fx.ControlKit.Editor</code>: a plain rounded textarea that reports every keystroke unless <code>BindOnChange</code> is set, adds <code>Cols</code>, <code>ReadOnly</code> and <code>Style</code>, and has no context menu, scroll-bar modes, typing modes or methods. With both namespaces imported, write the full name, as this page does with <code>Fx.ControlKit.TextAreaControl</code>.</p>
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-textareacontrol-events" Title="TextAreaControl events" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.TextAreaEvents.Length, "events")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Events" Title="TextAreaControl events" Rows="Vocab.TextAreaEvents" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-textareacontrol-methods" Title="TextAreaControl methods" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.TextAreaMethods.Length, "methods")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Methods" Title="TextAreaControl methods" Rows="Vocab.TextAreaMethods" />
                <p><code>CommitClientBufferedTypingAsync</code> is public only so the control's script can call it.</p>
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-textboxtypingbehavior" Title="TextBoxTypingBehavior" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Typing.Length, "values")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Values" Title="TextBoxTypingBehavior" Rows="Vocab.Typing" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-textareascrollbars" Title="TextAreaScrollBars" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.ScrollBars.Length, "values")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Values" Title="TextAreaScrollBars" Rows="Vocab.ScrollBars" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-textcontextmenuitems" Title="TextContextMenuItems" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.MenuItems.Length, "values")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Values" Title="TextContextMenuItems" Rows="Vocab.MenuItems" />
                <p>A <code>[Flags]</code> enum used by both <code>TextBoxControl</code> and <code>TextAreaControl</code>; combine members with <code>|</code>.</p>
            </DocSection>
        </DocSections>
    </Vocabulary>

    <Accessibility>
        <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Keyboard" Title="Keyboard" Rows="Vocab.Keys" />
        <ul>
            <li>All three render a native <code>&lt;input&gt;</code> or <code>&lt;textarea&gt;</code>, so the browser's own caret keys, selection and screen-reader announcements apply.</li>
            <li>None renders a label. <code>TextBoxControl</code> passes unmatched attributes such as <code>id</code>, <code>aria-label</code> or <code>aria-describedby</code> to its input. <code>NumericTextBoxControl</code> and <code>TextAreaControl</code> accept no unmatched attributes, and an <code>aria-label</code> on them fails when the page renders, so wrap them in a <code>&lt;label&gt;</code> as this page does.</li>
            <li><code>NumericTextBoxControl</code> sets <code>inputmode</code> to <code>numeric</code> or <code>decimal</code> for on-screen keyboards, and <code>aria-invalid="true"</code> while a <code>ValueChange</code> handler has cancelled the entry. Its spin buttons are hidden by its stylesheet.</li>
            <li><code>MaxLength</code> is enforced by the browser without a message. Show a count or a note, as the notes example does with a <code>role="status"</code> line.</li>
            <li>The password eye button has <code>aria-label</code> "Show password" or "Hide password" and <code>aria-pressed</code>; it is kept out of the Tab order (<code>tabindex="-1"</code>) so a form tabs as it would with a plain password box.</li>
            <li>The classic context menu opens on the browser's <code>contextmenu</code> event and is a list of plain buttons placed after the box, without menu roles. Escape does not close it; a click anywhere does.</li>
            <li>The classic scroll bar's arrow buttons are <code>aria-hidden</code> and out of the Tab order; the textarea itself still scrolls as the caret moves.</li>
        </ul>
    </Accessibility>

    <Related>
        <ul>
            <li>Text editors inside grid cells and the two typing transports: <a href="demo/grid/typing-modes">Typing modes</a>.</li>
            <li><code>FormControl</code> builds its text editors from <code>TextBoxControl</code> (<code>Multiline</code> for <code>FormEditorType.TextArea</code>): <a href="demo/forms">Forms</a>.</li>
            <li>Formatted text with toolbars: <a href="demo/rich-text-editor">Rich text editor</a>. Numbers picked by dragging: <a href="demo/sliders">Sliders</a>.</li>
        </ul>
    </Related>
</FeatureDemoLayout>

@code {
    // Traveller details
    private static readonly TravelData.Package Trip = TravelData.Packages[2];

    private string? _name = "Ana Moreira";
    private string? _email;
    private int _nameUpdates, _emailUpdates;
    private int _travellers = 2;
    private decimal _budget = 3200m;
    private string? _budgetNote;

    private void CountName() => _nameUpdates++;
    private void CountEmail() => _emailUpdates++;

    private void CheckBudget(NumericTextBoxControl<decimal>.NumericChangeEventArgs<decimal> e)
    {
        var floor = 250m * _travellers;
        if (e.Value < floor)
        {
            e.Cancel = true;
            _budgetNote = $"Budget not accepted: at least {floor:$#,##0} for {_travellers} travellers. The box keeps your figure until you change it.";
            return;
        }
        _budget = e.Value;
        _budgetNote = null;
    }

    // Notes with a limit
    private const int NoteLimit = 200;
    private Fx.ControlKit.TextAreaControl? _noteBox;
    private string? _note = "Arriving on the late flight on day one; please hold the room.";
    private bool _classicMenu;
    private string? _noteStatus;

    private int NoteLength => _note?.Length ?? 0;

    private async Task InsertTransfer()
    {
        if (_noteBox is null) return;
        var inserted = await _noteBox.InsertTextAsync("Airport transfer requested. ");
        _noteStatus = inserted ? "Inserted at the caret." : $"Not inserted: the phrase would pass the {NoteLimit}-character limit.";
    }

    private async Task FocusNote()
    {
        if (_noteBox is not null) await _noteBox.FocusAsync();
    }

    // Vocabulary rows, one per public member (FlexCore 0.2.49).
    private static class Vocab
    {
        public static readonly ApiRow[] TextBox =
        {
            new("Value", "The text. Bind with <code>@bind-Value</code>.", "string?", "null"),
            new("ValueExpression", "Set by <code>@bind-Value</code>. Server-backed edits then notify a surrounding <code>EditForm</code>'s <code>EditContext</code>. In the plain case (no <code>UpdateOnInput</code>, <code>OnKeyDown</code>, <code>InputValueChanged</code>, focus or selection options, classic menu or <code>ClientBuffered</code>) the control renders Blazor's own <code>InputText</code>, or <code>InputTextArea</code> when multi-line.", "Expression&lt;Func&lt;string?&gt;&gt;?", "null"),
            new("Placeholder", "Hint shown while the box is empty. An explicit <code>placeholder</code> attribute wins.", "string?", "null"),
            new("CssClass", "Class on the input, merged with any <code>class</code> attribute. Without one the input has no styling of its own; this page adds <code>text-field</code>.", "string?", "null"),
            new("Width", "CSS width written as an inline style, such as <code>250px</code> or <code>100%</code>. On a password box it sizes the wrapper and the input fills it.", "string?", "null"),
            new("Enabled", "False renders <code>disabled</code>. There is no <code>ReadOnly</code> parameter; a <code>readonly</code> attribute passes through to the input.", "bool", "true"),
            new("MaxLength", "Writes <code>maxlength</code>. A client-buffered commit is also cut to this length.", "int?", "null"),
            new("InputType", "The input's <code>type</code>: <code>email</code>, <code>tel</code>, <code>password</code> and so on. Ignored when <code>Multiline</code>; an explicit <code>type</code> attribute wins except for a password box.", "string", "\"text\""),
            new("Multiline", "Renders a <code>&lt;textarea&gt;</code> instead of an input.", "bool", "false"),
            new("Rows", "Writes the <code>rows</code> attribute: the visible lines of a multi-line box.", "int?", "null"),
            new("UpdateOnInput", "Raise <code>ValueChanged</code> on every keystroke instead of when the field changes.", "bool", "false"),
            new("TypingBehavior", "<code>ClientBuffered</code> keeps keystrokes in the browser and sends the whole value when the box loses focus; see the values table.", "TextBoxTypingBehavior", "TextBoxTypingBehavior.ServerBacked"),
            new("Uncontrolled", "The browser owns the text, so a parent re-render never writes older text back over what is being typed. False gives the controlled input whose value follows <code>Value</code> on every render.", "bool", "true"),
            new("ReseedOnOutsideChange", "When the parent sets a different <code>Value</code> from code, a browser-owned box shows it. Grid editors that push values through their own channel set this false.", "bool", "true"),
            new("AutoFocus", "Focuses the box after the first render and writes <code>autofocus</code>.", "bool", "false"),
            new("SelectOnFocus", "With <code>AutoFocus</code>, that first focus selects the text. On a later focus the control asks its script to select, and the script skips this whenever the text differs from the element's <code>value</code> attribute, which Blazor does not write, so a box holding text is not selected.", "bool", "false"),
            new("ReplaceOnFirstInput", "After the box gains focus, the first character typed replaces the whole text and the first Backspace or Delete clears it. A click inside the focused box cancels this.", "bool", "false"),
            new("SelectAllOnDoubleClick", "Double-click asks the script to select the whole text; the same <code>value</code>-attribute check as <code>SelectOnFocus</code> skips it for a box holding text.", "bool", "false"),
            new("UseClassicContextMenu", "Replaces the browser's right-click menu with the control's own Windows-style menu.", "bool", "false"),
            new("ContextMenuItems", "The items the classic menu shows; see the values table.", "TextContextMenuItems", "TextContextMenuItems.Legacy"),
            new("KeepNativeTab", "For <code>ClientBuffered</code> with an <code>OnKeyDown</code> handler: Tab commits and is reported once, but the browser still moves focus. Grid cell editors leave it false.", "bool", "false"),
            new("TypingKeysStayLocal", "Keydown events for printable keys, Backspace and Delete are not sent to the server; the text itself still is. Not used with <code>ClientBuffered</code>. For browser-owned editors whose host ignores typing keys, such as the grid's cell editor.", "bool", "false"),
            new("HtmlAttributes", "More attributes for the input, merged after the unmatched ones.", "Dictionary&lt;string, object&gt;?", "null"),
            new("ElementReferenceCaptured", "Called after each render with the input's <code>ElementReference</code>.", "Action&lt;ElementReference&gt;?", "null"),
            new("AdditionalAttributes", "Captures unmatched attributes (<code>id</code>, <code>aria-label</code>, <code>readonly</code>…) and writes them on the input.", "IDictionary&lt;string, object&gt;?", "null"),
